{
  "id": "m1-greetings",
  "title": "Greetings & Introductions",
  "summary": "Saying hello, asking how someone is, and introducing yourself.",
  "sections": [
    { "type": "text", "body": "<p>Arabic greetings often come in <strong>pairs</strong>: a set greeting and a set reply. Learn them together.</p>" },
    { "type": "table", "headers": ["Greeting", "Reply", "Meaning"], "arCols": [0, 1], "rows": [
      ["السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ", "وَعَلَيْكُمُ السَّلَامُ", "Peace be upon you / And upon you peace"],
      ["صَبَاحُ الْخَيْرِ", "صَبَاحُ النُّورِ", "Good morning / Morning of light"],
      ["مَسَاءُ الْخَيْرِ", "مَسَاءُ النُّورِ", "Good evening / Evening of light"]
    ] },
    { "type": "note", "body": "Arabic marks gender in “you”: <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.4rem'>أَنْتَ</span> anta to a man, <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.4rem'>أَنْتِ</span> anti to a woman. The same ending shows up in questions: <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.4rem'>كَيْفَ حَالُكَ</span> (to a man) and <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.4rem'>كَيْفَ حَالُكِ</span> (to a woman)." },
    { "type": "heading", "text": "A short dialogue" },
    { "type": "table", "headers": ["Arabic", "English"], "arCols": [0], "rows": [
      ["السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. اسْمِي أَحْمَد. مَا اسْمُكَ؟", "Peace be upon you. My name is Ahmed. What's your name?"],
      ["وَعَلَيْكُمُ السَّلَامُ. اسْمِي يُوسُف.", "And upon you peace. My name is Yusuf."],
      ["كَيْفَ حَالُكَ؟", "How are you?"],
      ["بِخَيْرٍ، الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ. وَأَنْتَ؟", "Fine, praise be to God. And you?"]
    ] }
  ],
